## Context

Third round of live findings, testing v0.3.18 right after install. All
wording, layout, and rendering-cost findings — no correctness bugs this
round.

## Findings and fixes

1. **The switch-state line and the raw "State: {phase}" line were separate
   and disconnected.** Merged into one sentence: "Indexing is on/off." plus
   a phase-specific clause. Every reachable phase gets a plain-language
   second half (idle, scanning, extracting, an unexpected error, or a
   resource-blocked reason reusing the toolbar tooltip's own wording so the
   two never say the same fact two different ways). The raw phase name moved
   to Technical diagnostics ("Internal phase: {phase}"), for debugging.
2. **"Census: {scanned} / {total}"** reworded to "Scanned {scanned}
   attachments out of {total}."
3. **The census table had no visual separation from the readings above it,
   and no rule setting the total off from the category rows it sums.** The
   table now carries margin above and below; the total row's cells get a
   top border, applied only when there is more than one row.
4. **The "Overall progress" heading grew a library-name list that wrapped
   five lines deep on a narrow window with three long library names.** Moved
   the scope out of the bold `<legend>` (frozen at build time, message id
   alone now) into a plain line of its own (`sdt-scope`), which wraps like
   any other sentence and is recomposed on every render exactly as before.
5. **The Details layer visibly blinked between documents.** `renderState()`
   rebuilt the whole census `<table>` via `replaceChildren` on every 100 ms
   tick regardless of whether the account had actually changed — almost
   always, since a real document transition is a small minority of ticks.
   Memoized per dialog (a signature stored on the dialog object, since two
   open windows must each fill their own table on first render even if they
   happen to agree) and skipped when the account is unchanged.

## Test

- `tests/sdt_sitter_dialog.mjs`: every reachable phase's merged switch line,
  driven through `describeSDTSwitchLine`; the total row's border and the
  table's margin; the internal-phase debug line; the scope line's new
  location and the heading's now-static text, with a mock `Libraries.getAll`
  added to exercise it; node-identity proof that the census table only
  rebuilds on a real change (verified red against the pre-fix code by
  temporarily disabling the memoization guard, and separately for the scope
  fix via `git stash`).
- `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py`: three tests updated for the moved scope
  line and its own `_site` anchors; one `UI_SITES` entry retargeted.

## Verification

- [x] All four `.mjs` suites pass
- [x] `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py`, `tests/test_sitter_host_apis.py` pass
- [x] `make check-fast` — 1311 passed, 1 pre-existing environmental failure
      (podman rootless-container store, unrelated, documented this session)
- [x] Manifest/update.json bumped 0.3.18 -> 0.3.19, version guard clean
- [x] Both the memoization fix and the scope-line move verified with a
      positive control (red against the pre-fix behavior)

## Exit criteria

The switch line names the phase in one sentence for every reachable phase.
The census table carries visible separation and a total rule, without
rebuilding on ticks where nothing changed. The scope line wraps normally
regardless of how many libraries are named.
